                        "username": "PatrickLinww"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz, this change implements part of the design document discussed earlier (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/84016).\nWhen you have time, could you please take a look and share your feedback? Thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "debug-monitor/debug-monitor.cpp",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "whats wrong with std::chrono::duration?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "debug-monitor/debug-monitor.cpp",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "whats wrong with sdbusplus here? Why are we using the raw bindings?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "debug-monitor/debug-monitor.cpp",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "whats wrong with ofstream?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "debug-monitor/debug-monitor.cpp",
                    "line": 112,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "seems like we should be using RAII here, which I believe sdbusplus gets us. In any case, if thats not usable for som reason consider just wrapping this in an raii class like (similar to GSL's final_action https://github.com/microsoft/GSL/blob/main/include/gsl/util#L98C1-L99C1:\n\n\ntemplate<typename FunctorCleanup>\nclass OnScopeExit {\npublic:\n    OnScopeExit() = delete;\n    explicit OnScopeExit(FunctorCleanup &&f) : f{f} {}\n    ~OnScopeExit(){\n        f();\n    }\n    OnScopeExit& operator=(const OnScopeExit&) = delete;\n    OnScopeExit(const OnscopeExit&) = delete;\n    OnScopeExit(OnScopeExit&&) = delete;\n    OnScopeExit& operator=(OnSecopeExit&&) = delete;\nprivate:\n    FunctorCleanup f; \n};\n\ntemplate <typename F>\nauto makeOnscopeExit<F>(F &&f)\n{\n    return OnScopeExit<F>(std::forward(f));\n}\n\nint run()\n{\n    auto cleanup = makeOnscopeExit(<your existing lambda>);\n}\n\nthat said, please just use the existing RAII handlers if possible."
                }
            ],
